@startuml sequence-ocr-job-lifecycle
!include elvira.iuml
' =============================================================================
' What: an OCR job (#146, first IP-031 kind) has two independent sources of
'       truth that the ledger joins by task id: Celery events say where the task
'       is (queued, received, started, succeeded, failed, revoked), the worker's
'       report says what it produced; only the report changes the acquisition,
'       and the changed file re-queues LCP encryption and extraction as child jobs.
' Kind: UML sequence diagram, proposal (IP-031). Scope: start, run, report,
'       follow-up jobs, failure + retry, revoke. Omitted: authentication details,
'       telemetry spans, the sweeper (a job with no event past its time limit
'       becomes lost), how LCP and extraction themselves run.
' Source: apps/tasks/management/commands/celery_event_handler.py;
'         apps/core/models/acquisition.py background_tasks; evilflowers-ocr-worker
'         ef4311d evilflowers_ocr_worker/__init__.py; apps/readium/views/hooks.py
'         (report pattern, #99); EvilFlowersCatalog#146 (2026-11-14).
' =============================================================================

title OCR job lifecycle: start, events, report, follow-ups, retry and revoke (proposal, 2026-11-14)

actor "Admin\nelvira-portal" as admin
participant "catalog API\n/api/v1/jobs" as api
participant "JobService\n+ OcrKind" as svc
database "Ledger\npostgresql18" as ledger
queue "Redis db 7" as redis
participant "ocr worker" as worker
participant "Event listener\nevilflowers-beat" as listener

== start ==
admin -[$accent_msg()]> api : <b>POST /api/v1/jobs</b>\n{kind: files.ocr, subject: acquisition}
api -> svc : start(kind, subject, user)
svc -> svc : permission · eligible?\n(PDF, language, no active job)
svc -[$accent_msg()]> ledger : <b>INSERT job (status queued)</b>
svc -> redis : on commit: send_task(\n…ocr, task_id = job.id)
api --> admin : 201 {job: queued}

== run (Celery events) ==
redis -> worker : consume
worker -> redis : task-received · task-started
redis -> listener : events (celeryev)
listener -> ledger : UPDATE status received → started\n(event timestamp, worker, attempt)
worker -> worker : ocrmypdf(skip_text)\n→ catalogs/…/ocr/{job}.pdf

== report (domain outcome) ==
worker -[$accent_msg()]> api : <b>POST /api/v1/jobs/{id}/report</b>\n{output, pages, pages_ocred}
api -> svc : report(job, payload)
svc -> ledger : UPDATE report, reported_at;\nacquisition gets the new file + checksum
svc -> ledger : INSERT child jobs (parent = job):\nreadium.encrypt · extraction.run
svc -> redis : send_task(child tasks)
api --> worker : 200
worker -> redis : task-succeeded (runtime, result)
redis -> listener : event
listener -> ledger : UPDATE status succeeded

== failure and retry ==
worker -> redis : task-failed (exception, traceback)
redis -> listener : event
listener -> ledger : UPDATE status failed, error, traceback
admin -> api : POST /api/v1/jobs/{id}/retry
api -> svc : retry(job)
svc -> ledger : INSERT job (retry_of = id, queued)
svc -> redis : send_task(new task_id)

== revoke ==
admin -> api : POST /api/v1/jobs/{id}/revoke\n{terminate}
api -> svc : revoke(job)
svc -> ledger : UPDATE revoke_requested_at
svc -> redis : control.revoke(task_id)\n(pidbox broadcast)
redis -> worker : revoke
worker -> redis : task-revoked
redis -> listener : event
listener -> ledger : UPDATE status revoked

caption Celery events and the worker's report are separate: events drive the status, the report drives the change\nto the acquisition. A report without task-succeeded (or the reverse) is visible in the ledger instead of lost.\nEvery start, retry and follow-up writes its ledger row before the task is sent, so nothing runs unrecorded.
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · EvilFlowersCatalog · docs/diagrams/sequence-ocr-job-lifecycle.puml
@enduml
